{"type":"after","callId":"call@225","endTime":49306.003,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/The arm sequence — from $CLEAR to a live gun\n    \n\nThe arm sequence — from  to a live gun\nThe exact frame order that takes a tagger live, respawns it, and ends the game — captured from the official app and reproduced by our host\n👥communityLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\nThis sequence was captured from the official iOS app driving a live game on firmware v4.32, then reproduced byte-for-byte by our own host on real taggers. Three pieces were missing from every earlier attempt:  after spawn,  before and after spawn, and the empty token in .Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e, §7o; protocol/captures/2026-08-23-ios-callsign-game-start.txt\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e, §7k\nDEV-04diagram pendingSequence diagram: host → gun frames above, with the gun's echoes ( after ;  after ;  per shot;  per trigger).Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e\nWhat the gun echoes back\n\n\nAfter\nEcho\nMeaning\n\n\n\n\n\nCleared state\n\n\n\n\nLive: HP 45, armor 70, mag 36, reserve 216 (this config)\n\n\neach shot\n …\nMag decrementing, slot 0, reserve, heat\n\n\neach trigger\n / \nPress / release\n\n\n~30 s\n\nTelemetry continues in-game\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e\nThe config head is silent and safe.Writing  without  plays nothing and a configured-but-unspawned gun ignores IR — no , no . \"Get some\" and the cocking sound belong to . A head held unspawned for ~2 minutes then spawned went live with config intact.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7r\nDeath and respawn are host-driven\nVictim reports  then . The gun does not revive itself, and a dead gun's trigger produces  events but no  decrement (it cannot fire).\nThe app sends  ~1.7 s after death.\nAfter the game's respawn delay (the app's own timer — ~10 s in the capture; 👥community community: a per-death ramp capping at 45/90 s) the host sends .\nGun echoes  — HP, armor and ammo restored with no  needed.\nA dead gun ignores all incoming IR — 448 distinct words, including every grenade-beacon shape, failed to revive one. Only the host can.\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7f, §7j(community ramp), §7q; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-26 448-word brute force)\nAfter a BLE drop, re-send the whole head.Re-sending the full sequence (→→…→→) on a fresh link brought a gun back in every bench case.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7r and §7r addendum\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e, §7n, §7o\nDo I need the reload-handle pull?No. The manual's reload-handle pull is the local start;  is the remote one. Both exist.\nWhere do respawn time, game time, lives and score-to-win go?Nowhere on the gun. Three captures at respawn 5/15/30 s gave byte-identical /. Your host keeps the clock.\nIs the second  (after ) needed?Yes — omit it and the trigger is dead.\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e · protocol/brx-protocol.md §7n · protocol/brx-protocol.md §7e, §7r addendum\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@225"}
